In article <1991Jul23.140137.19381@mcs.anl.gov> shaclark@mcs.anl.gov (Shannon Clark i.e. Quietus) writes:
>
>I have a simple question for all you people out there.  I have been trying to  
>determine the abilities and advantages to the different modes of play. I mean  
>Wizard Mode, Explore Mode and just regular mode.

In Explore Mode you get a wand of wishing and the option of not dying.  In
Wizard Mode you _don't_ get a wand of wishing, but you don't need it because
you can wish for an item whenever you want to by pressing ^W.  (You can even
wish for a blessed +100 gray dragon scale mail and get it.  None of this
wimpy +3 stuff! :-) ) Wizard Mode also has some other nifty commands:

^G: create a monster
^F: magic map level
^V: level teleport

and so on.  You can get a list of all of them by pressing ? and selecting
"Wizard Mode commands."

I strongly advise you NOT to play in Wizard Mode.  It will be fun at first,
but it will quickly ruin your game.

BTW, on Unix systems only one user is allowed to become Wizard.  If you
got a wand of wishing in Wizard Mode and didn't see any difference from
Explore Mode, you were probably actually in Explore Mode.  If so, ignore
everything I said.

